The check for multi-values in the `percentileBlock` can be simplified by combining conditions:
```java
if (percentileBlock.isNull(p) || percentileBlock.getValueCount(p) != 1) {
    if (percentileBlock.getValueCount(p) > 1) {
        warnings.registerException(new IllegalArgumentException("single-value function encountered multi-value"));
    }
    result.appendNull();
    continue position;
}
```
This reduces the nesting level and makes the code easier to follow.
